WEBVTT

00:20.850 --> 00:26.820
If I was dreaming, how did I forget?

00:26.890 --> 00:30.660
It pulsed through me, frigid, shocked me

00:30.660 --> 00:32.300
Can I do, do?

00:32.960 --> 00:37.960
I want you next to me when I summon you

00:39.130 --> 00:42.970
Waiting close by, but you seem far off

00:42.970 --> 00:45.310
Na, na, na, knight

00:45.310 --> 00:48.480
The more beautiful the rose

00:48.480 --> 00:51.450
The more its thorns hurt

00:51.450 --> 00:54.720
Now that I'm strong

00:54.720 --> 00:59.720
My heart knows to protect that vow

01:00.720 --> 01:03.760
Let's meet in the dark of night

01:03.760 --> 01:06.830
Where you're waiting

01:06.830 --> 01:09.830
You'll worship the cruel Dark Queen

01:09.830 --> 01:13.000
Who's drunk with danger

01:13.000 --> 01:15.970
You shattered the glass sword

01:15.970 --> 01:18.940
You wielded without thinking

01:18.940 --> 01:21.880
Its shards glow in the night

01:21.880 --> 01:25.350
I lick your wounded fingers

02:02.620 --> 02:04.120
Hey, Hime?

02:04.120 --> 02:05.550
What?

02:05.550 --> 02:07.490
Isn't that a distress signal?

02:07.490 --> 02:09.160
Distress signal?

02:09.160 --> 02:11.330
Yeah, sounds like it's coming from out at sea.

02:11.330 --> 02:13.140
What should we do?

02:38.350 --> 02:39.990
Huga.

02:48.800 --> 02:52.600
The distress signal came from near here.

02:52.600 --> 02:54.970
I don't see anything that looks like a vessel.

02:54.970 --> 02:57.350
There's nothing on the radar.

02:58.970 --> 03:01.420
Could it have sunk already?

03:08.520 --> 03:11.390
My goodness...
Where did that come from?

03:11.390 --> 03:13.590
It's not being picked up on the radar, either!

03:13.590 --> 03:14.920
What?!

03:14.920 --> 03:16.290
We're gonna hit it!

03:16.290 --> 03:18.660
Full speed to port!

03:18.660 --> 03:20.730
No good! We won't make it in time!

03:33.510 --> 03:35.280
They're gonna sink.

03:35.280 --> 03:38.880
Yeah, just like what happened to us.

03:38.880 --> 03:42.550
We received a distress signal while cruising,

03:42.550 --> 03:46.820
suddenly it appeared out of nowhere
at sea and caused us to sink.

03:46.820 --> 03:50.130
It's sending out distress signals
in order to sink ships?

03:51.390 --> 03:52.530
Liza?

03:52.530 --> 03:56.360
A flute, I hear a flute playing.

03:56.360 --> 03:57.900
A flute?

03:57.900 --> 04:00.140
I don't hear anything.

04:01.270 --> 04:04.410
They say that dogs' hearing ability is
many times stronger than humans'.

04:04.410 --> 04:06.070
I'm a wolf!

04:06.070 --> 04:08.150
I wonder if someone's in there?

04:08.940 --> 04:11.310
We'll know when we go in there and look around.

04:11.310 --> 04:12.310
Let's go.

04:12.310 --> 04:14.080
What? We're going to look in there?!

04:14.080 --> 04:19.400
Of course, we have no way
of going home, anyway.

04:41.010 --> 04:43.390
Doesn't look like anyone's here.

04:44.450 --> 04:47.360
Is this a luxury liner?

04:47.950 --> 04:50.930
Correction, it used to be a luxury liner.

04:55.360 --> 04:58.130
Looks like it's been here for years.

04:59.660 --> 05:02.530
Not all of its fittings have gone bad.

05:02.530 --> 05:05.480
Hey, Hime, isn't this, you know...

05:06.330 --> 05:12.550
A mysterious ghost ship, full of riches,
that went missing, etc.

05:17.710 --> 05:19.520
A werewolf?!

05:20.920 --> 05:23.900
I'll explain later; look behind you!

05:34.460 --> 05:36.270
Take that!

05:52.510 --> 05:54.820
But you knocked him out.

05:54.820 --> 05:56.890
Are these guys undead?

05:57.520 --> 05:59.330
This Way!

06:04.160 --> 06:06.140
God, you're annoying!

06:12.470 --> 06:15.870
Damn it, what are those guys?

06:15.870 --> 06:17.370
Are we safe?

06:17.370 --> 06:19.270
They won't break that door easily.

06:19.270 --> 06:25.250
Young lady, a werewolf warrior should
never retreat from an enemy.

06:25.450 --> 06:28.620
You won't be able to protect your master like that!

06:29.480 --> 06:32.560
I... I'm nobody's servant!

06:33.150 --> 06:35.460
Ex..Excuse me.

06:35.460 --> 06:40.460
I'm Lisa Wildman, daughter of the mighty warrior,
Worg Wildman.

06:41.400 --> 06:43.030
Worg?

06:43.400 --> 06:45.470
Do you know my father?

06:45.730 --> 06:49.570
We fought together in the battle on Gagalph Hill.

06:49.570 --> 06:51.550
He was quite the soldier.

06:52.240 --> 06:57.690
I'm Keziah Bold, son of the mighty warrior,
Kedaria Bold.

06:58.450 --> 07:01.120
I see, you're Worg's daughter.

07:01.120 --> 07:04.420
I had heard he had taken a human spouse.

07:04.420 --> 07:06.790
I hate to interrupt this little chat,

07:06.790 --> 07:10.320
but can you tell us what's going on here,
Keziah, or whatever your name is?

07:10.330 --> 07:12.560
My sincere apologies.

07:12.560 --> 07:14.970
I see I'm in the presence of a princess.

07:24.710 --> 07:29.010
So, you came here the same way we did, Keziah?

07:29.010 --> 07:32.780
Yes, our boat sank three days ago,
after the collision.

07:32.780 --> 07:35.020
I am the sole survivor.

07:35.020 --> 07:38.090
Is this really safe to eat?

07:38.090 --> 07:40.320
I found it in the galley.

07:40.320 --> 07:42.670
Don't eat it if you don't want to, human.

07:46.560 --> 07:48.860
So, there's no one on board?

07:48.860 --> 07:51.400
I've only encountered ghosts so far.

07:51.400 --> 07:53.500
But there's one oddity...

07:53.500 --> 07:55.040
The flute?

07:55.040 --> 07:56.100
Yes...

07:56.100 --> 07:57.740
Wait!

07:58.070 --> 08:01.180
Can you hear it now, Keziah?
The flute's playing again.

08:03.780 --> 08:05.610
I can.

08:05.610 --> 08:08.620
Perhaps there's a survivor left on board.

08:16.730 --> 08:18.530
Guys, look!

08:22.900 --> 08:25.570
It's a ship! We should yell for help!

08:25.570 --> 08:28.340
They can't see this ship from there.

08:29.300 --> 08:33.340
It's heading here,
because it picked up the distress signal,

08:33.340 --> 08:37.240
but just like us, it's going to collide and sink.

08:37.250 --> 08:39.750
Then, what should we do?

08:39.750 --> 08:41.560
Isn't it obvious?

08:43.320 --> 08:45.550
We're going to look for a mermaid.

08:45.550 --> 08:46.890
A mermaid?

08:46.890 --> 08:49.370
Aren't they all but extinct now?

08:51.330 --> 08:56.030
Yes, mermaids are known for
calling ships with flutes.

08:56.030 --> 08:59.270
If we follow the flute, we can find them.

08:59.270 --> 09:01.580
Though they're the root of all this evil,

09:02.240 --> 09:07.350
they're also the angels who can
rescue us from this ship.

09:56.890 --> 09:58.870
Hime, what are those?

09:59.490 --> 10:02.460
Those are the souls of those taken by this ship.

10:02.460 --> 10:05.130
They're excited because they have new recruits.

10:05.130 --> 10:07.230
Then, those guys before...

10:07.240 --> 10:08.900
They're mostly likely the evil undead.

10:08.900 --> 10:11.670
Damn, no wonder they wouldn't die.

10:11.670 --> 10:13.880
They're already dead!

10:24.390 --> 10:27.490
Hey, were you waiting for us?

10:27.490 --> 10:29.300
I'll see you off.

10:31.960 --> 10:35.530
You should be able to take them if you charge in,

10:35.530 --> 10:37.510
if you're a real werewolf warrior.

10:38.370 --> 10:42.170
You've got that right, Your Highness!

10:42.170 --> 10:45.070
Follow my lead, Liza, daughter of Worg!

10:45.070 --> 10:46.710
Okay!

11:09.600 --> 11:11.700
One after another!

11:13.740 --> 11:15.370
Damn!

11:21.540 --> 11:23.350
Damn you!

11:24.610 --> 11:27.410
I thought he was a soldier of the Royal Family!

11:27.420 --> 11:29.450
Pretty weak for a soldier!

11:30.490 --> 11:32.890
This isn't the time for insults!

11:32.890 --> 11:36.090
What? Complaining already?

11:36.090 --> 11:38.230
I'm just getting started!

11:38.230 --> 11:39.860
All right, let's go!

11:57.110 --> 11:58.280
Huga.

11:58.280 --> 12:00.580
Hmm? Oh, right.

12:00.580 --> 12:02.750
Hiro and the others aren't back yet.

12:02.750 --> 12:05.590
Maybe they ended up in another country.

12:05.590 --> 12:07.230
Huga.

12:12.760 --> 12:16.330
Flan, want to make an even bigger sand castle?

12:16.330 --> 12:17.830
Huga.

12:17.830 --> 12:21.440
We could use some more sand.
Can you take care of that?

12:21.440 --> 12:23.420
Coming right UP!

12:25.640 --> 12:27.280
Huga.

12:31.680 --> 12:34.280
I can hear the flute now, too.

12:34.280 --> 12:36.380
Yeah, it's quite close.

12:36.380 --> 12:37.650
Hey, you okay?

12:37.650 --> 12:39.460
Shut up.

12:39.590 --> 12:42.230
I hate to admit it, but it's true.

12:42.760 --> 12:45.240
His strength is the real deal.

12:45.630 --> 12:48.440
I'd expect nothing less from
a comrade of my father.

12:49.530 --> 12:51.800
So, this is it.

12:51.800 --> 12:54.470
It's locked from the outside, huh?

12:54.470 --> 12:56.900
So, it's sealed in.

12:56.910 --> 12:58.890
I think I see what's going on here.

13:05.110 --> 13:08.190
So, where's this mythical mermaid?

13:15.790 --> 13:19.260
Your Highness, I hate to be the
bearer of bad news,

13:19.260 --> 13:21.970
but this kid has legs.

13:23.870 --> 13:27.440
No, I understand what happened.

13:29.300 --> 13:34.300
She's a mermaid that traded her voice for a
curse that gave her a human body.

13:35.840 --> 13:37.480
What?

13:37.650 --> 13:42.650
She can neither swim away nor can she scream.

13:42.850 --> 13:47.990
She was stuck in here, playing that flute,
calling ships here to rescue her.

13:48.660 --> 13:52.030
You mean that curse that says
she'll die if she speaks?

13:52.030 --> 13:55.230
Makes sense she'd be locked in.

13:55.230 --> 13:56.870
Damn!

14:00.370 --> 14:02.350
It's okay now.

14:02.500 --> 14:05.070
I'll get you out of here.

14:05.070 --> 14:06.370
No, you won't.

14:06.370 --> 14:08.010
Huh?

14:08.410 --> 14:10.720
I need you to do something.

14:11.480 --> 14:16.350
This ship is using that mermaid's
power to summon boats here

14:16.350 --> 14:20.720
to cause disasters at sea
in order to devour people's souls.

14:20.720 --> 14:22.700
We have to sink it.

14:26.490 --> 14:29.760
We have to get off this ship right away, Liza.

14:29.760 --> 14:31.300
Don't tell me what I have to do!

14:31.300 --> 14:33.280
I won't let go of you.

14:37.110 --> 14:39.070
We have to hurry, he's coming.

14:39.070 --> 14:40.610
He?

14:40.610 --> 14:43.250
That mermaid has been allowing him to prosper.

14:43.610 --> 14:47.680
He won't let us take her away.
He'll come after her.

14:49.250 --> 14:51.060
After her?

14:51.750 --> 14:53.660
The leader of the evil spirits.

14:54.690 --> 14:57.360
In other words, our main foe.

15:00.230 --> 15:02.040
Liza, follow me.

15:13.040 --> 15:14.640
This...

15:14.640 --> 15:19.320
You know where the room where they
keep the canned goods is, right?

15:20.650 --> 15:23.250
Sink the ship, eh?

15:23.250 --> 15:28.250
Well, Your Highness, I want to see
what you're capable of.

15:29.960 --> 15:34.410
I need to see if you pose a threat to my master.

15:41.470 --> 15:42.700
Ah, damn it!

15:42.700 --> 15:45.450
Seems he doesn't want us to escape!

15:51.850 --> 15:54.760
Okay, the rest is up to you.

15:59.720 --> 16:01.700
It's starting to sink.

16:12.970 --> 16:14.950
Liza, in here!

16:23.480 --> 16:25.460
Did that stop him?

16:26.610 --> 16:28.420
I don't know.

16:35.690 --> 16:37.290
What's with this thing?!

16:37.290 --> 16:38.560
He. S comin Q!

16:38.560 --> 16:41.130
Damn, what should we do?

16:41.130 --> 16:42.770
This.

17:08.390 --> 17:10.200
What's happening?

17:11.630 --> 17:15.270
The souls he captured are being released.

17:33.350 --> 17:35.380
In the legend of the mermaid,

17:35.380 --> 17:40.920
it is said she made a deal to become human
in order to be with her lover.

17:41.560 --> 17:48.670
The sound of your flute may have given
solace to the soul of your beloved.

17:51.630 --> 17:55.640
Don't just stand there! The ship's about to sink!

17:56.300 --> 17:58.000
Not a problem.

17:58.010 --> 18:02.810
But we'll be dragged to the bottom of the ocean.

18:02.810 --> 18:04.540
It doesn't matter.

18:04.550 --> 18:08.580
Even if we sink, this mermaid will
call someone to rescue us.

18:11.020 --> 18:12.790
Oh...

18:18.330 --> 18:21.600
Instead of that, how about
you be honest with us?

18:22.160 --> 18:27.070
You originally came to this ship
to protect the mermaid, did you not?

18:27.070 --> 18:28.880
Who sent you?

18:30.170 --> 18:31.980
It was...

18:33.070 --> 18:34.880
Watch out!

18:38.010 --> 18:39.550
She spoke?

18:39.550 --> 18:43.320
Fool! If a cursed mermaid speaks, she'll...

18:43.320 --> 18:44.960
...die.

18:48.320 --> 18:50.130
What on Earth?!

18:50.560 --> 18:52.540
Keziah, it's too late!

18:58.100 --> 19:01.410
Goddamn it! I'm such an idiot!

19:06.370 --> 19:10.690
Royalty has the ability to grant
half-immortality to the dead.

19:10.810 --> 19:13.620
I shall grant her my Flame of Life.

19:17.080 --> 19:19.560
Serve me for all eternity.

19:27.900 --> 19:29.530
Master...

19:31.030 --> 19:33.000
You bastard! You're royalty?!

19:33.000 --> 19:34.810
Liza, stop!

19:44.880 --> 19:46.280
Liza!

19:46.280 --> 19:48.560
It's fine, she's not dead.

19:49.280 --> 19:51.090
He went easy on her.

19:54.690 --> 19:57.140
Liza, daughter of Worg,

19:58.330 --> 20:01.800
next time I see you in battle,
I will not take pity on you.

20:07.400 --> 20:09.070
Brother...

20:17.040 --> 20:20.080
You're calling ships for my younger sister?

20:21.720 --> 20:23.530
What a good girl.

20:28.190 --> 20:30.790
For the sake of my little soldier here,

20:30.790 --> 20:32.930
I'll allow you to escape today.

20:33.890 --> 20:37.900
Are you implying you can kill me
whenever you want to?

20:37.900 --> 20:39.200
Yes.

20:39.200 --> 20:43.040
Emile, my older brother, let me say this...

20:43.040 --> 20:46.110
I have no interest in the throne.

20:48.140 --> 20:51.010
However, I have no interest in dying, either.

20:51.010 --> 20:55.120
So, in order to survive, we may have
to cross swords someday.

20:58.720 --> 21:01.100
You haven't changed a bit.

21:05.830 --> 21:10.060
All we were after today
was protecting the mermaid.

21:10.060 --> 21:11.930
Let's go, Flanders.

21:11.930 --> 21:13.570
Huga.

21:23.110 --> 21:26.560
I finally found out today

21:27.180 --> 21:31.100
exactly what sort of war Hime is involved in.

21:41.160 --> 21:42.970
A rescue ship?

22:13.030 --> 22:18.030
Get down on your knees and lick my red nails

22:18.600 --> 22:26.540
Call me queen with your entangled tongue

22:29.110 --> 22:31.880
The sun that blooms in Hell

22:31.880 --> 22:34.610
Darkness that's fallen to Paradise

22:34.620 --> 22:37.180
If you're confronted with light and despair

22:37.180 --> 22:39.820
Which one goes deeper?

22:39.820 --> 22:42.560
Roses fly from my head

22:42.560 --> 22:45.260
I'll scatter them into Nirvana

22:45.260 --> 22:47.860
Wounds that secretly pain you

22:47.860 --> 22:50.430
Blood that gushes away

22:50.500 --> 22:53.130
They both lead to the depths of my heart

22:53.130 --> 22:55.800
You've given these gorgeous gifts as tribute

22:55.800 --> 22:58.470
And yet you're still

22:58.470 --> 23:01.170
Seeking love?

23:01.180 --> 23:03.910
Tell me exactly to what extent

23:03.910 --> 23:06.580
Grown men are just foolish little boys?

23:06.580 --> 23:11.580
Get down on your knees and lick my sacred feet

23:11.850 --> 23:16.850
Call me queen in your hoarse voice

23:17.290 --> 23:22.290
The proof of your life creeps up the tower of pain

23:22.530 --> 23:25.230
Slowly making your way, you can barely breathe

23:25.230 --> 23:27.870
But if you still ask for it

23:27.870 --> 23:31.840
Your dying breath just might be

23:31.840 --> 23:40.120
The words that melt my frozen tears

23:41.350 --> 23:42.350
Huga.

23:42.350 --> 23:44.650
This is bad! There's some weirdo with a whip!

23:44.650 --> 23:45.650
A whip?

23:45.650 --> 23:48.390
Yes! He's lashing the heck out of me!

23:48.390 --> 23:50.990
With a whip? Like this? Or that?

23:50.990 --> 23:53.330
That hurts, Hime! Don't hit me for real!

23:53.330 --> 23:54.760
I said that hurts!

23:54.760 --> 23:57.600
Oh, hit me more... more...

23:57.600 --> 23:58.430
Huga.

23:58.430 --> 24:00.870
Eww, no, Flandre, I was just joking.

24:00.870 --> 24:03.500
Don't give me that cold look.

24:03.500 --> 24:05.710
Next episode, "Princess Connection"

24:05.710 --> 24:07.840
Were you really joking?

24:07.840 --> 24:09.310
Not you too, Hime?

24:09.310 --> 24:10.790
Huga, huga.
